The LLM reviewer left this comment on line 81
(category: bug, severity: medium):

`IgnoreFailures` only ignores failures that the delegate reports inside the returned `DeletionResult`. An `IOException` thrown by `delegate.delete(...)` propagates out of this method unchanged, so deletion failures surfaced as exceptions (the declared `@throws IOException in case of general failures`) are not ignored. If the intent is "never fail the test because of cleanup", the delegate call should be wrapped in a try/catch and logged like the unsuccessful-result case.

